<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William, Count of Schaumburg-Lippe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1724–1777</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Wilhelm of Schaumburg-Lippe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William was count of Schaumburg-Lippe from 1748 to 1777 and a noted military reformer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a>. He commanded the Allied artillery in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> and in 1762 reorganised the Portuguese army against a Spanish invasion. At home he built the island fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelmstein">Wilhelmstein</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steinhuder-meer">Steinhuder Meer</a> and a military school there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-count-of-schaumburg-lippe.jpg" alt="William, Count of Schaumburg-Lippe" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Georg Ziesenis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wilhelm_(Schaumburg-Lippe).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
